{"id": "2026-10-18-news-france-counts-damage-after-riots", "date": "2026-10-18", "stream": "news", "headline": "France counts damage after riots", "summary": "Nationwide cost-of-living protests in France on 17 October ended in riots, looting and 1,800 arrests.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/news/international/wir-haben-die-schnauze-voll-sichtbare-schaeden-nach-protesttag-in-frankreich", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["politics", "world"], "importance": 3, "display_body": "French Interior Minister Laurent Nuñez said on Sunday 18 October that 1,800 people were arrested and 500 police officers and firefighters were injured during Saturday's nationwide protests against the cost of living, which turned into the worst riots in France in years. Nuñez put the number of protesters at 550,000; the CGT union said 800,000. The marches were called on social media under the slogan \"On en a marre!\" (\"We're fed up\") by former Yellow Vests, school and university students, farmers and unions, and were followed by looting and arson in Paris, Lyon, Strasbourg and other cities. In Paris alone police made 855 arrests, which the police prefecture called a \"record\"; the Paris prosecutor said 517 people were held in custody, 171 of them minors. In Lyon, the regional prefect said a peaceful march of about 20,000 people was \"very quickly\" overtaken by violent groups and then by looters, and the tourist office on Place Bellecour was set on fire. Smaller protests against high prices also took place in Italy, Portugal and Belgium.", "why": "the unrest comes six months before France's presidential election, and Prime Minister Sébastien Lecornu's government faces broad anger over fuel, food and energy prices, school shortages and farm incomes.", "thread_id": "2026-10-18-news-france-counts-damage-after-riots", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-18", "event_date": "2026-10-17", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["France", "Laurent Nuñez", "CGT", "Sébastien Lecornu"]}
{"id": "2026-10-18-news-babi-s-ano-wins-no-czech-senate-seats", "date": "2026-10-18", "stream": "news", "headline": "Babiš's ANO wins no Czech Senate seats", "summary": "Opposition-linked candidates won 22 of 27 Czech Senate seats, leaving PM Babiš's ANO without a single new seat.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/populist-czech-pm-babis-goes-empty-handed-in-senate-elections/a-79690934", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["politics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Czech Prime Minister Andrej Babiš's ANO movement failed to win a single seat in the Senate election run-offs held on Friday 16 and Saturday 17 October, and opposition parties kept their majority in the upper house. Candidates linked to the opposition won 22 of the 27 seats up for election in the 81-member Senate; the centrist parties STAN and ODS did best. ANO stays at 14 senators. Babiš said his party \"certainly didn't expect\" to win nothing, but that his government would continue its programme, including an unpopular plan to change how public broadcasters are funded. It was the first national vote since ANO won the lower-house election in October 2025.", "why": "the lower house makes most laws, but the Senate must approve constitutional changes and Constitutional Court judges, so it can block the government's plans for the public media and the courts.", "thread_id": "2026-10-18-news-babi-s-ano-wins-no-czech-senate-seats", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-18", "event_date": "2026-10-17", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Czech Republic", "Andrej Babiš", "ANO", "Czech Senate"]}
{"id": "2026-10-18-news-deadly-fire-at-canadian-army-base", "date": "2026-10-18", "stream": "news", "headline": "Deadly fire at Canadian army base", "summary": "A fire at CFB Wainwright in Alberta killed and injured several people on 17 October, Canada's defence minister said.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/18/deaths-injuries-after-fire-at-alberta-military-base-canada-minister", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["world"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "A fire at Canadian Forces Base Wainwright in Alberta killed and injured several people on Saturday 17 October, Canada's defence minister David McGuinty said, without giving numbers. Strong winds carried the fire beyond the base, one of Canada's busiest military training areas, into the surrounding countryside. Global News, citing unnamed military sources, reported at least seven dead and dozens injured, and said a gas line or gas well was hit during live-fire training, causing an explosion; these details have not been confirmed officially . An emergency doctor in Edmonton, 180 km from the base, told CBC that hospitals near the base were \"completely overwhelmed\" and called it \"a one in every 15-to-25-year disaster\". Prime Minister Mark Carney spoke of a \"serious incident\".", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-10-18-news-deadly-fire-at-canadian-army-base", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-18", "event_date": "2026-10-17", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Canada", "CFB Wainwright", "David McGuinty", "Mark Carney"]}
{"id": "2026-10-18-news-settlers-attack-european-diplomats-in-west-bank", "date": "2026-10-18", "stream": "news", "headline": "Settlers attack European diplomats in West Bank", "summary": "Masked Israeli settlers attacked European diplomats, a French mayor and an archbishop in Taybeh on 17 October.", "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/17/israeli-settlers-attack-european-diplomats-in-west-bank", "source_domain": "theguardian.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Masked Israeli settlers attacked European diplomats, a French mayor and the archbishop of Cambrai during the olive harvest in Taybeh, in the occupied West Bank, on Saturday 17 October, injuring three people. The group of about seven men, some carrying clubs, knocked down Bernard Baudoux, mayor of Aulnoye-Aymeries in northern France, and smashed a window of an armoured car of the Belgian mission; the French consul general and the Belgian and Polish consuls were present. Belgian Foreign Minister Maxime Prévot condemned the attack and said Belgium would keep pushing for EU sanctions on settlers. Israeli police opened an investigation, while Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's office spoke of a \"smear\" campaign against settlers. The Israeli rights group Yesh Din counts more than 170 settler attacks since the harvest began on 27 September. On Saturday, US Secretary of State Marco Rubio said Washington had asked Israel to \"crack down\" after a US photojournalist was beaten by settlers on Friday 16 October; he did not mention that President Trump lifted US sanctions on violent settlers on his first day back in office in January 2025.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-10-18-news-settlers-attack-european-diplomats-in-west-bank", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-18", "event_date": "2026-10-17", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["West Bank", "Israel", "Taybeh", "Belgium", "Marco Rubio"]}
{"id": "2026-10-18-news-sisi-offers-to-defend-saudi-arabia", "date": "2026-10-18", "stream": "news", "headline": "Sisi offers to defend Saudi Arabia", "summary": "Egypt's President Sisi said Egypt would help defend Saudi Arabia against Houthi attacks if asked and sought parliament's approval.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/egypt-s-ssisi-says-he-ll-defend-saudi-arabia-if-asked/a-79689105", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Egypt's President Abdel Fattah al-Sisi said on Saturday 17 October that Egypt was ready to help defend Saudi Arabia if asked, and asked parliament to meet in an emergency session to authorise it. \"I'm not talking about fighting anyone or attacking anyone. We are speaking only about defense,\" Sisi said at a military academy ceremony. The session was expected on Sunday 18 October. Yemen's Iran-backed Houthis have stepped up attacks on Saudi Arabia, including on energy sites and Riyadh's main airport; one attack a week ago killed 13 people, the deadliest in the kingdom in more than a decade. Egypt was part of the Saudi-led coalition that entered Yemen's war in 2015.", "why": "Egyptian forces in Saudi Arabia would widen a regional war that is already pushing up energy prices worldwide.", "thread_id": "2026-10-18-news-sisi-offers-to-defend-saudi-arabia", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-18", "event_date": "2026-10-17", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Egypt", "Abdel Fattah al-Sisi", "Saudi Arabia", "Houthis"]}
{"id": "2026-10-18-news-rubio-says-starshield-off-limits-to-ukraine", "date": "2026-10-18", "stream": "news", "headline": "Rubio says Starshield off-limits to Ukraine", "summary": "Rubio said Ukraine has no access to SpaceX's military Starshield network and denied the US ordered a Starlink slowdown.", "url": "https://www.state.gov/releases/office-of-the-spokesman/2026/10/secretary-of-state-marco-rubio-remarks-to-the-press-18/", "source_domain": "state.gov", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["official PR"], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Masked Israeli settlers attacked European diplomats, a French mayor and the archbishop of Cambrai during the olive harvest in Taybeh, in the occupied West Bank, on Saturday 17 October, injuring three people. The group of about seven men, some carrying clubs, knocked down Bernard Baudoux, mayor of Aulnoye-Aymeries in northern France, and smashed a window of an armoured car of the Belgian mission; the French consul general and the Belgian and Polish consuls were present. Belgian Foreign Minister Maxime Prévot condemned the attack and said Belgium would keep pushing for EU sanctions on settlers. Israeli police opened an investigation, while Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's office spoke of a \"smear\" campaign against settlers. The Israeli rights group Yesh Din counts more than 170 settler attacks since the harvest began on 27 September. On Saturday, US Secretary of State Marco Rubio said Washington had asked Israel to \"crack down\" after a US photojournalist was beaten by settlers on Friday 16 October; he did not mention that President Trump lifted US sanctions on violent settlers on his first day back in office in January 2025.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-10-18-news-rubio-says-starshield-off-limits-to-ukraine", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-18", "event_date": "2026-10-17", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Marco Rubio", "Ukraine", "Starshield", "Starlink", "SpaceX"]}
{"id": "2026-10-18-news-efta-and-vietnam-sign-free-trade-deal", "date": "2026-10-18", "stream": "news", "headline": "EFTA and Vietnam sign free trade deal", "summary": "Switzerland, Norway, Iceland and Liechtenstein signed a free trade agreement with Vietnam in Hanoi on 18 October.", "url": "https://www.efta.int/media-resources/news/efta-and-viet-nam-sign-free-trade-agreement", "source_domain": "efta.int", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["new source"], "topics": ["switzerland", "economy"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Switzerland, Norway, Iceland and Liechtenstein signed a free trade agreement with Vietnam in Hanoi on Sunday 18 October, more than a decade after talks began in 2012. President of the Confederation Guy Parmelin signed for Switzerland as head of the economics department, and Vietnam's Minister of Industry and Trade signed for Vietnam. The agreement removes or cuts customs duties and also covers services, investment, intellectual property, public procurement and sustainable development. Trade between the four EFTA countries and Vietnam was worth €4.8 billion in 2025, with a €2.5 billion surplus in Vietnam's favour (Swiss figures exclude gold). EFTA's main exports to Vietnam are electrical machinery, fish and medicines; its main imports are electrical machinery, shoes and clothing. On Saturday 17 October Parmelin met President Tô Lâm, and both sides said they want to finish talks on a new investment-protection agreement.", "why": "before it takes effect, the deal needs approval by the Swiss parliament, and it can be challenged by referendum, as happened this week with the EFTA agreement with Malaysia.", "thread_id": "2026-10-18-news-efta-and-vietnam-sign-free-trade-deal", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-18", "event_date": "2026-10-18", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["EFTA", "Vietnam", "Switzerland", "Guy Parmelin"]}
{"id": "2026-10-18-news-riniker-wins-aargau-government-seat", "date": "2026-10-18", "stream": "news", "headline": "Riniker wins Aargau government seat", "summary": "FDP national councillor Maja Riniker was elected to the Aargau cantonal government on 18 October.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/news/schweiz/aargauer-regierungswahl-maja-riniker-ist-neue-regierungsraetin", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland", "politics"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "FDP national councillor Maja Riniker was elected to the Aargau cantonal government on Sunday 18 October, with 70,137 votes, well ahead of the other candidates. She replaces Stephan Attiger (FDP), who leaves at the end of the year, and is expected to take over the department of construction, transport and environment. Riniker, president of the National Council in 2025, was also backed by the SVP and Die Mitte; the SP supported Juso candidate Loredana Nigro. The GLP candidate Dominik Gresch withdrew earlier after reports about tax debts.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-10-18-news-riniker-wins-aargau-government-seat", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-18", "event_date": "2026-10-18", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Maja Riniker", "Aargau", "FDP"]}
{"id": "2026-10-18-news-switzerland-updates-maduro-asset-freeze-list", "date": "2026-10-18", "stream": "news", "headline": "Switzerland updates Maduro asset-freeze list", "summary": "Switzerland removed two people and added six, including Alex Saab, to its asset-freeze list of Maduro associates.", "url": "https://www.letemps.ch/articles/la-suisse-ajuste-la-liste-des-proches-de-nicolas-maduro-aux-avoirs-bloques", "source_domain": "letemps.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Switzerland updated its list of people close to former Venezuelan president Nicolás Maduro whose assets are frozen, removing two names and adding six, in a list published on Friday 16 October. The list now has 41 names. Alex Saab, a businessman and former industry minister, and his associate Álvaro Pulido Vargas were added; both were recently expelled to the United States by the government of interim president Delcy Rodríguez. The wife of Interior Minister Diosdado Cabello and the Chavista lawmaker Jorge Arreaza, who leads the parliamentary committee on Venezuela's amnesty law, were removed. The foreign ministry did not comment on individual cases. The list was first drawn up on 5 January, after Maduro was captured in a US military operation in Caracas.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-10-18-news-switzerland-updates-maduro-asset-freeze-list", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-18", "event_date": "2026-10-16", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Switzerland", "Venezuela", "Nicolás Maduro", "Alex Saab"]}
